ollowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bigtreetech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bigtreetech/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bigtreetech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bigtreetech/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bigtreetech/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bigtreetech/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bigtreetech/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bigtreetech/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/x-compressed","state":"uploaded","size":607621428,"digest":"sha256:df016c18383c6b9ddc2fe285636911624d2692d5b0dbd5c13ecf9fa5dc15d258","download_count":1885,"created_at":"2025-08-21T07:58:13Z","updated_at":"2025-08-21T08:05:46Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/bigtreetech/CB2/releases/download/V3.0.2/CB2_Debian12_minimal_kernel6.1_20250821.img.xz"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigtreetech/CB2/tarball/V3.0.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigtreetech/CB2/zipball/V3.0.2","body":"# Image\r\n\r\n## Version 20250429/20250529\r\n### Changelog\r\n * Fix the issue of GPU/NPU driver not loading due to incorrect kernel configuration.\r\n * Add startup from PCIe(NVMe) feature in u-boot. RK3566 won't boot directly from NVMe, so we need to write u-boot to the SD Card or eMMC first. After u-boot start up, u-boot can boot the Linux from NVMe. Please follow the steps below:\r\n   * Start the system from the SD card first.\r\n   * Erasing the entire eMMC to prevent the system from booting from eMMC, as eMMC has a higher startup priority than NVMe\r\n    `sudo mkfs /dev/mmcblk1`\r\n   * Only write u-boot to eMMC\r\n    `sudo armbian-install`\r\n    select\r\n    `Install/Update the bootloader on eMMC (/dev/mmcblk1)`\r\n   * Shut down the system after the installation of uboot is completed\r\n    `sudo poweroff`\r\n    * Remove the SD card and hold down the `Recovery` button, And then power on, the uboot in eMMC will treat NVMe as a USB Mass Storage. And then writing system to NVMe just like writing to eMMC through a computer.\r\n    * After writing, modify your custom configuration in the `/boot` partition, then power off and restart to start Linux through NVMe\r\n \r\n### Known issues\r\n* When playing audio through HDMI, there will be no audio output for the first 1-2 seconds, It will be normal after 1-2 seconds\r\n* Some users have reported that the system encounters a [problem when enabling the Obico service](https://github.com/bigtreetech/CB2/issues/88), so a temporary system image without built-in Obico service is provided(`CB2_Debian12_Klipper_kernel6.1_20250529_without_obico.img.xz`). If you do not need to use the Obico service, it is recommended to prioritize using this image\r\n\r\n\r\n## Version 20250821\r\n### Changelog\r\n* Fixed the issue of abnormal startup on Manta M5P, may also fixed https://github.com/bigtreetech/CB2/issues/101 and https://github.com/bigtreetech/CB2/issues/92","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bigtreetech/CB2/releases/215720957/reactions","total_count":19,"+1":10,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":9}}